:: StoryInterface
<!--
	Story chrome — two display modes around the story's single #passages
	element. RAW HTML: SugarCube wraps this content in its own #story element
	(authoring another one here is fatal) and does not process macros.
	SugarCube 2.37 requires exactly one #passages inside a custom
	StoryInterface — this is the story's one and only; every passage renders
	inside it.

	Shell mode (default; the title and any non-checker passage): the compact
	rail panel beside a centered reading card (shell.css).

	Stage mode ([checker] passages that are not [title]; gated on the passage
	tag classes SugarCube puts on <body>): the letterboxed .stage frame
	(stage.css), aspect-locked to the 2840:1700 design canvas. Five slots:
	the background — #tmem-bg, the existing animated checkerboard, declared
	here and letterboxed into the same box by checker.css
	the three content slots below, empty until the content macros fill them;
	and the menu — the same .rail, repositioned by stage.css into the stage's
	menu slot.

	The rail is a sibling of .shell rather than a child, so one element serves
	as the shell's rail and the stage's menu. It is position: fixed in both
	modes, and stage.css repositions it.

	Wiring: rail links carry data-shell-action and are handled in shell.js,
	which resolves SugarCube's API at click time. Inline onclick cannot work
	here: SugarCube 2.37.3 exposes UI / Engine / State / Story on
	window.SugarCube only — there are no bare globals to reach from an inline
	handler.
-->
<!-- first child of the StoryInterface: the background layer, letterboxed
     into the stage box by checker.css. Declared here rather than built by JS
     so the page has a background on first paint — it is the only page
     background in shell mode — and so the pattern is markup a redesign edits
     rather than DOM a script fabricates. -->
<div id="tmem-bg"><div class="pattern"></div></div>
<div class="shell">
	<div class="main">
		<div id="passages"></div>
	</div>
</div>
<aside class="rail">
	<h1 class="rail-title">Cam Safety</h1>
	<nav class="rail-actions">
		<a href="#" title="Settings" data-shell-action="settings"><span class="rail-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#9881;</span> Settings</a>
		<a href="#" title="Saves" data-shell-action="saves"><span class="rail-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#128190;</span> Saves</a>
		<a href="#" title="Restart" data-shell-action="restart"><span class="rail-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#8635;</span> Restart</a>
		<!-- Prev/next, disabled: remove the comment markers below to re-enable (one line) -->
		<!-- <a href="#" title="Previous passage" data-shell-action="back"><span class="rail-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#8249;</span> Back</a> <a href="#" title="Next passage" data-shell-action="forward">Next <span class="rail-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#8250;</span></a> -->
	</nav>
</aside>
<div class="stage">
	<div class="stage-slot stage-cam" data-stage-slot="cam" data-slot-label="Cam portrait"></div>
	<div class="stage-slot stage-bubble" data-stage-slot="bubble" data-slot-label="Cam speech-bubble"></div>
	<div class="stage-slot stage-reply" data-stage-slot="reply" data-slot-label="Player reply bar"></div>
</div>